Z||000000||vEnOm||09-05-2001||12:44 PM||||Im planning to install a transmission oil cooler with a 10in x 10in fan in front of the A/C condenser. Is it possible to connect it in the same relay of the Radiator fan? Will it damage the relay? Please help!<P>vEnOm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><BR>87 Nitrous Project ||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||09-05-2001||12:46 PM||||How many amps is the fan going to draw on full speed?  Do you only want the tranny cooler fan to come one when the rad. fan is?  If you want to be able to control the tranny fan yourself just hook it up to a separate relay and switch.||||reg||1
Z||000002||vEnOm||09-05-2001||12:55 PM||||Well actually Im putting 1 separate switch for both fans. That way I can turn them on when there is heavy traffic and use them on normal operation at Highway speed. Don't know yet how many amps its going to draw. I will find out and post it. I just want to make sure it doesn't damage my new fan relay.<P>Thanx FieroJoe||||reg||1
Z||000003||vEnOm||09-05-2001||01:07 PM||||Oh by the way. I want them to turn on at the same time. That way it wil make a better cooling effect for the Radiator.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||09-05-2001||01:32 PM||||Well, if it isnt going to pull more than 10 amps, you might be able to get away with just splicing it into the output of the relay.  If you have a single speed fan in your car they should be brown and red wires.  brown goes to the fan, red is hot at all times.||||reg||1
